caption: Talent Gate and Negation Caps
tradition-component: talent-gate-and-negation-caps

A Dreadhound may only construct a negation ability from a Power or Anti-Power for which the character actually possesses the governing Power Talent or Anti-Talent at Basic level. A Pattern or prey repository never grants the governing Talent.

Anti-Talents purchased for Dreadhound do not count against the character's normal Will/5 limit on Basic or secondary Psi Talents. Unless another rule explicitly says otherwise, they still obey the normal level and access limits for Basic or secondary Talents.

When an ability is loaded through Dreadhound Super-Memorization, use twice the character's actual purchased level in its governing Talent as the Talent-equivalent for Talent-based level, damage, magnitude, and similar caps. This is a cap calculation only. It does not increase the Talent, add to rolls, change the ability's access band, improve permanent abilities, or satisfy prerequisites that require a particular Talent level.
